  "slug": "spin-altermagnetism-d7e3",
  "summary": "Eight preprints propose transport, optical and magnonic signatures that identify and exploit altermagnetic, odd-parity, noncoplanar and spin-nematic order.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is theory that ties measurable responses to the symmetry of unconventional magnetic order. For altermagnets, noncoplanar antiferromagnets and odd-parity magnets, the proposed probes are octupolar magneto-optical effects, nonlinear spin generation and spin photocurrent, and charge-spin selection rules with temporal-spectral separation in transport. Twist engineering of collinear bilayers is proposed to give quasicrystalline altermagnets with high-order spin polarization. On the magnon side, single magnons and bound magnon pairs in pyrochlore spin-nematics give competing thermal Hall contributions that allow field-tunable sign reversal. In CrI3 nanotubes, an axial field produces a conical phase and a large pseudo-orbital magnon moment. In BiFeO3, gate-controlled domain boundaries modulate nonreciprocal magnons in a proposed transistor. Cavity photon condensation driven by scalar spin chirality is a more peripheral item. All eight are preprints.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-23"
}
